  "facts": {
    "law": "Law 11: offside position = any part of head, body or feet in the opponents' half (not the halfway line) and nearer the goal line than both the ball and the second-last opponent, judged when a team-mate plays/touches the ball; hands/arms of all players incl. keepers not considered; level = onside; no offence from goal kick, throw-in, corner; position alone is not an offence (must interfere with play/opponent or gain advantage)",
    "1990": "level made onside by IFAB in 1990 after Italia 90 (2.21 goals per game, lowest World Cup average)",
    "1925": "three -> two opponents, June 1925, effective 1925/26; First Division goals up 42.3%",
    "mccracken": "Newcastle full-back Bill McCracken perfected the offside trap",
    "saot": "Premier League semi-automated offside first used 12 Apr 2025 (Man City v Crystal Palace); up to ~30 cameras under the roof track the ball and thousands of data points per player"
  },
